  {
    "number": 143,
    "title": "Record 85HA keyboard and N30 mouse qualification findings",
    "body": "The owner's packaging identifies an 8BitDo N Edition keyboard (85HA) and N30 mouse (85CA). The earlier R8 research lead does not describe this mouse. This candidate records the actual hardware, cited per-control/per-connection capabilities, Windows/Wispr/Codex interfaces, mapping ownership and a reversible operator trial.\n\nRefs #64. This is the source-evidence candidate; #64 remains incomplete and #65 remains blocked. The keyboard's genuine held output, N30 event identities/selective suppression, installed app versions and a complete supported route are unqualified. No input observer, mapping write, microphone use, app dispatch or installation ran. Read-only Windows inventory failed because this session could not execute Windows tools.\n\nThe canonical desktop-control document and generated guide incorporate the new evidence. Guide inputs reconcile concurrent #63 closure and merged source history. Public guide publication remains separate.\n\nValidation on the committed candidate:\n\n- Node 24: `npm run check:workflow` and `npm run test:workflow` passed; 11 specifications, 10 archives and 15 workflow tests. This documentation introduces no behavior or wire-contract delta, so no new OpenSpec capability is needed.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py`: all five tests passed.\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs`: coverage, links, navigation, interactions and print restoration passed at six widths. Desktop/mobile/print renders were inspected. The guide covers 95 open issues, 130 linked issues, 52 roadmap nodes and nine diagrams.\n- All nine Archify artifacts passed 9/9 deterministic checks; guide regeneration produced no drift. The standalone desktop-input viewer still fails its viewport check for vertical overflow, with identical dimensions and diagnostics to the previous artifact. This existing limitation is retained, not reported as a pass.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews, including Windows/input compatibility, and all six applicable hosted jobs are pending. Merge eligibility depends on their results and the missing qualification evidence; this PR has no automatic issue-closure keyword. Source work does not establish installed, application or physical acceptance.\n",
    "state": "open",
